- @backSpecialScene: Exit library.

@government
go-to: menu

[? if not national_congress_seen : The <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#008C45">Kingdom</span> <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CFCFCF">of</span> <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CD212A">Italy</span>, also known as <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#008C45">It</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CFCFCF">a</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CD212A">ly</span>, is a Constitutional Monarchy under a King and a Bicameral Parliament, composing the appointed Senate and the elective Chamber of Deputies. The Chamber is responsible for governing, while the King has a largely ceremonial role as well as a few important responsibilities.  ?]

[? if violent_revolution : The Soviet Republic of italy, also known as Italy, is a Soviet Republic under a Prime Minister and the Supreme Soviet, the legislative body of the Soviet Republic. ?]

[? if peaceful_revolution : The Republic of Italy, also known as Italy, is a Parliamentary Republic under a Prime Minister and a Bicameral Parliament, composing both the elected Senate and elected Chamber of Deputies. The Chamber is responsible for governing, while the Prime Minister is elected via the governing coalition. ?]

[? if not violent_revolution : The Chamber of Deputies is elected based on a proportional representation voting system, apportioning 508-535 seats based on the D'Hondt method, added alongside newly introduced universal male suffrage. The King then appoints the Prime Minister and Cabinet, usually under the request of the Chamber of Deputies. A majority vote-of-no-confidence can remove the current government, though a new coalition is typically formed utilising the same composition of the Chamber of Deputies. ?]

[? if violent_revolution : The Supreme Soviet is elected based on a proportional representation voting system, typically with voters choosing a candidate from the [+ psi_full_name +], appointing a total of 508-535 seats. Newly added universal male suffrage has expanded voting blocs exponentially. ?]

<span style="font-weight: bold; color:#008C45">It</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CFCFCF">a</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CD212A">ly</span> is divided into a number of states, each of which have their own governments with some responsibilities, albeit insignificant.


@italy_timeline
go-to: menu

= Timeline of the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#ED2855">[+ psi_name +]</span> and the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#008C45">Kingdom</span> (until 1919)

**1861**: The <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#008C45">Kingdom</span> <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CFCFCF">of</span> <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CD212A">Italy</span> is officially unified and established as a nation-state under a Constitutional Monarch.

**1892**: The <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#ED2855">[+ psi_name +]</span> is officially founded in Genoa, caused by the rise of labour, socialism and dissatisfaction with the political system. It is divided between the Reformists & Revolutionaries, growing throughout the rest of the Century into a coalition of Communists to Social Democrats.

**1898**: Protests are violently suppressed by the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#008C45">It</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CFCFCF">al</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CD212A">ian</span> government, leading to political radicalisation of the working class and an increase in <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#ED2855">[+ psi_name +]</span> popularity.

**1900**: King Umberto I is assassinated by an anarchist, further heightening tensions.

**1914**: World War One begins. Parties are divided on the Italian stance towards the war, though the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#ED2855">[+ psi_name +]</span> adopts a neutrality stance against the war and opposes any intervention in the conflict.

**1915**: <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#008C45">It</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CFCFCF">a</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CD212A">ly</span> joins World War One on the side of the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#C8102E">Ent</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#000091">ente</span> after signing the Treaty of London. The <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#ED2855">[+ psi_name +]</span> fractures as more radical members support the war whilst others remained anti-war, resulting in members like Benito Mussolini being kicked out of the party.

**1917**: Increased war exhaustion and discontent increases the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#ED2855">[+ psi_name +]</span>'s popularity, as many become frustrated with <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#008C45">It</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CFCFCF">a</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CD212A">ly</span>'s involvement in World War One.

**1919**: World War One ends.

[? if peaceful_revolution : **[+ rev_year +]** - <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#008C45">It</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CFCFCF">a</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CD212A">ly</span> abolishes the Monarchy via constitutional reformation and establishes a republic. ?]

[? if violent_revolution : **[+ rev_year +]** - The <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#008C45">Kingdom</span> <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CFCFCF">of</span> <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CD212A">Italy</span> is violently overthrown by left-wing forces that establish a Italian socialist republic. ?]

