@demographics
go-to: menu

**Demographic Groups**

**Urban Workers**: Consisting of blue-collar workers in factories, workshops, mines, et cetera. Most are <span style="color:#ED2855">socialists</span>, supporting the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#ED2855">[+ psi_name +]</span> or any other communist faction. They make up about 20 to 25% of the population.

**Small Business Owners**: Consisting of shopkeepers, artisans, small business workers and the like. They are divided between the <span style="color:#87CEFA;">Catholic</span> Parties, <span style="color:#0047AB;">Libe</span><span style="color:#FFD700;">ral</span> Parties and a small minority to the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#ED2855">[+ psi_name +]</span>. They make up about 15-20% of the population.

**Rural Workers & Farmers**: Consisting of those who lived in the unindustrialised south who work as farmers, agricultural workers, et cetera. They are fairly evenly split between the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#ED2855">[+ psi_name +]</span> and the <span style="color:#87CEFA;">Catholic</span> <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#87CEFA;">PPI</span>. They make up about 50% of the population.

**Industrialists & Landowners**: Consisting of the elite holding significant economic power. They are the bedrock of the <span style="color:#0047AB;">libe</span><span style="color:#FFD700;">ral</span> parties, seeing them as stable and protecting their wealth, though some more religious prefer the <span style="color:#87CEFA;">Catholic</span> parties. They make up about 5-10% of the population.

**Veterans & Unemployed**: Consisting of veterans who felt betrayed by the government for their gains in the First World War. They are fierce supporters of <span style="color:#522A00">nationalist</span> and <span style="color:#3D3D3D;">fascist</span> movements, though some opted to support the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#ED2855">[+ psi_name +]</span> instead. They make up about 5% of the population.

**Catholics**: Consisting of the clergy and those religious to the Catholic Church. They support the <span style="color:#87CEFA;">Catholic</span> parties almost entirely, making up a strong foundation for the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#87CEFA;">PPI</span>. They make up about 5% of the population.

