@parties
go-to: menu

<span style="font-weight: bold; color:#ED2855">[+ psi_name +]</span> - *[+ psi_full_italian +]* ([+ psi_full_name +]) - This is you. You are the major <span style="color:#ED2855">socialist</span> party of the working class, founded by labour movements and socialist ideas. [? if not communist_split and not reformists_defect and not violent_revolution : Currently, the party is split between those who wish to preserve the parliamentary system and those who wish to achieve <span style="color:#ED2855">socialism</span> through a revolution. ?] [? if reformists_defect and not communist_split and not violent_revolution : Currently, the party's direction has shifted towards the end of the <span style="color:#0047AB;">bou</span><span style="color:#FFD700;">rge</span><span style="color:#1E99C5;">ois</span> state through revolutionary action. What shall become of the revolution beyond the current state's collapse, however, is not yet decided. ?] [? if not reformists_defect and communist_split and not violent_revolution : Currently, the party's direction has shifted towards a parliamentary reformist movement towards <span style="color:#ED2855">socialism</span>, working with the opposition to democratize and socialize society. With both the King's approval and the Senate, the party will push for a complete constitutional overhaul. ?] [? if reformists_defect and communist_split and not violent_revolution : Currently, the party is merely struggling to survive, a husk of its former self. What remains of the party is scrambling towards whatever path will save them, while some have already left the seemingly sinking ship. ?] [? if violent_revolution and not communist_split : Embracing the ideological line of the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CE0000">Communist International</span>, the party has morphed into a revolutionary vanguard which steers the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#008C45">It</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CFCFCF">al</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CD212A">ian</span> nation to a new socialist future. ?] [? if violent_revolution and communist_split : Embracing a more independent ideological line diverging from that of the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CE0000">Communist International</span>, the party seeks to emulate it's own variant of a socialist republic instead of following Moscow's vision. ?]

[? if pcdi_formed : <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#C72F35">PCd'I</span> - *Partito Comunista d'Italia* (Communist Party of Italy) - A splinter party of the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#ED2855">[+ psi_name +]</span>, formed after the <span style="color:#8B0000">left</span> wing of the party and its leaders split. ?]

[? if pcdi_formed : Current relations: [+ pcdi_relation : relationships +] ?]

[? if psu_formed : <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#E35A5A">PSU</span> - *Partito Socialista Unitario* (Unitary Socialist Party) - A splinter party of the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#ED2855">[+ psi_name +]</span>, formed after the <span style="color:#FF6961">reformist</span> wing of the party and its leaders split. ?]

[? if psu_formed : Current relations: [+ psu_relation : relationships +] ?]

[? if not psri_collapse : <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#FFC0CB;">PSRI</span> - *Partito Socialista Riformista Italiano* (Italian Reformist Socialist Party) - A splinter of reformists from the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#ED2855">[+ psi_name +]</span>, the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#FFC0CB;">PSRI</span> are a centre-left party, advocating for socialism through the parliamentary system. ?]

[? if not psri_collapse : Current relations: [+ psri_relation : relationships +] ?]

[? if pll_formed : <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#FFD1D9;">PLL</span> - *Partito Liberale dei Lavoratori* (Liberal Workers' Party) - A splinter of the left-wing of the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#1E99C5;">[+ ds_name +]</span>. The <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#FFD1D9;">PLL</span> are a left-wing <span style="color:#0047AB;">libe</span><span style="color:#FFD700;">ral</span> party under the leadership of Vincenzo Giuffrida, attempting to uphold the legacy of Giuseppe De Felice Giuffrida's *Fasci Siciliani*. ?]

[? if pll_formed : Current relations: [+ pll_relation : relationships +] ?]

[? if pri_prominent : <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#3CB371">PRI</span> - *Partito Repubblicano Italiano* (Italian Republican Party) - A centre-left party formed in 1895, the party holds its roots in <span style="color:#3CB371">Republicanism</span> and the ideals of men such as Giuseppe Mazzini and Giuseppe Garibaldi. ?]

[? if pri_prominent : Current relations: [+ pri_relation : relationships +] ?]

<span style="font-weight: bold; color:#1E99C5;">[+ ds_name +]</span> - *[+ ds_full_italian +]* ([+ ds_full_name +]) - [? if ds_party : A newly formed centre-left party under the merger ?][? if not ds_party : A newly formed electoral list consisting ?] of the Constitutional Democratic Party, the Democratic Party and the People's Democratic Party and others. Its electoral list is supported mainly by the the Southern regions of Italy.

Current relations: [+ ds_relation : relationships +]

<span style="font-weight: bold; color:#87CEFA;">PPI</span> - *Partito Popolare Italiano* (Italian People's Party) - A newly formed Christian Democratic party under the merger of UECI, FUCI, CC and the PPT. The party has its support rooted in the Clergy, Rural Workers and Middle Class.

Current relations: [+ ppi_relation : relationships +]

<span style="font-weight: bold; color:#FFD700;">[+ ldr_name +]</span> - *[+ ldr_full_italian +]* ([+ ldr_full_name +]) - A recently formed [? if ldr_party : centre party ?][? if ldr_list : electoral list ?] under the merger of the Liberal Democratic Party, the Radical Liberal Party and others. They get their support mainly from the industrialists & Landowners under the leadership of Vittorio Emanuele Orlando, former Prime Minister.

Current relations: [+ ldr_relation : relationships +] 

<span style="font-weight: bold; color:#0047AB;">[+ ul_name +]</span> - *[+ ul_full_italian +]* ([+ ul_full_name +]) - A centre-right party that remained as remnants of the party that refused to merge to form the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#FFD700;">[+ ldr_name +]</span>, led by Giovanni Giolitti.

Current relations: [+ ul_relation : relationships +]

[? if pcs_formed : <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#656573;">PCS</span> - *Partito Cristiano Sociale* (Christian Social Party) - A splinter of the right-wing of the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#1E99C5;">[+ ds_name +]</span>. The <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#656573;">PCS</span> are a right-wing <span style="color:#0047AB;">libe</span><span style="color:#FFD700;">ral</span> party under Gabriello Carnazza and adovcates for cooperation with the far-right against the left. ?]

[? if not pnf_banned : <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#3D3D3D;">[+ pnf_name +]</span> - *[+ pnf_full_italian +]* - ([+ pnf_full_name +]) - A newly formed organisation, operating essentially as the political expression of [+ pnf_leader +]'s <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#3D3D3D;">Fasces of Combat</span>. ?]

[? if not pnf_banned : Current relations: [+ pnf_relation : relationships +] ?]

**Other parties** - There is a multitude of small parties, such as the Economic Party, the Italian Republican Party, Independent Socialists, and others. Their positions usually covers the political spectrum from the left to the right.

@paramilitaries
on-arrival: {!
Q.rg_strength = Math.round(Q.rg_strength);
Q.fdc_strength = Math.round(Q.fdc_strength);
Q.ard_strength = Math.round(Q.ard_strength); 
Q.adp_strength = Math.round(Q.adp_strength);
Q.abl_strength = Math.round(Q.abl_strength);
!}
go-to: menu

**Paramilitary groups:**

[? if not national_congress_seen : **<span style="color:#c2352b">Red Guards</span>**: The <span style="color:#c2352b">Red Guards</span> are a paramilitary group most associated with the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#ED2855">[+ psi_name +]</span>, organising strikes, factory occupations as well as conflict with right-wing militias, most active in the Northern regions of Italy. ?]

[? if not national_congress_seen : Strength: [+ rg_strength +] thousand ?]

[? if not national_congress_seen : Militarization: [+ rg_militancy : militancy +] ?]

[? if arditi_formed : **<span style="color:#2F2F2F">Arditi</span> <span style="color:#3CB371">del</span> <span style="color:#ED2855">Popolo</span>**: The <span style="color:#2F2F2F">Arditi</span> <span style="color:#3CB371">del</span> <span style="color:#ED2855">Popolo</span> are a broad anti-fascist group, formed to combat the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#3D3D3D;">Fasci</span>. They are made up of anarchists, <span style="color:#8B0000">communists</span>, <span style="color:#ED2855">socialists</span>, <span style="color:#3CB371">republicans</span>, <span style="color:#2F2F2F">syndicalists</span>, and everything in between. ?]

[? if arditi_formed : Strength: [+ adp_strength +] thousand ?]

[? if arditi_formed : Militarization: [+ adp_militancy : militancy +]?]

[? if not national_congress_seen : <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#3D3D3D;">Fasci Italiani di Combattimento</span>: The <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#3D3D3D;">Fasci</span> are a paramilitary group headed by [+ pnf_leader +], and frequently come into conflict with the <span style="color:#c2352b">Red Guards</span>. ?]

[? if not national_congress_seen : Strength: [+ fdc_strength +] thousand ?]

[? if not national_congress_seen : Militarization: [+ fdc_militancy : militancy +] ?]

[? if not national_congress_seen : **<span style="color:#3D3D3D;">Arditismo</span>**: The <span style="color:#3D3D3D;">Arditismo</span> are a paramilitary group allied with the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#3D3D3D;">Fasci</span>, operating as an independent group frequently coming into conflict with the <span style="color:#c2352b">Red Guards</span> as well. ?]

[? if not national_congress_seen : Strength: [+ ard_strength +] thousand ?]

[? if not national_congress_seen : Militarization: [+ ard_militancy : militancy +] ?]

[? if not national_congress_seen : **<span style="color:#3D3D3D;">Anti-Bolshevik Leagues</span>**: The <span style="color:#3D3D3D;">Anti-Bolshevik Leagues</span> are a group of local organisations opposed to <span style="color:#ED2855">socialism</span> and created in direct response to the Biennio Rosso, funded primarily by landowners and industrialists. ?]

[? if not national_congress_seen : Strength: [+ abl_strength +] thousand ?]

[? if not national_congress_seen : Militarization: [+ abl_militancy : militancy +] ?]

**Official military/paramilitary groups:**

[? if not national_congress_seen : **<span style="color:#008C45">Regi</span><span style="color:#CFCFCF">o Eser</span><span style="color:#CD212A">cito</span>**: ?][? if national_congress_seen : **Esercito Italiano**: ?] [+ army_strength +] thousand troops. This is <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#008C45">It</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CFCFCF">a</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CD212A">ly</span>'s army, still mobilised after the First World War.

Loyalty: [+ army_loyalty : loyalty +]

**<span style="color:#FF2400">Carabinieri</span>**: [+ interior_police_strength +] thousand members. This is the forces of the Interior Ministry.

Loyalty: [+ interior_police_loyalty : loyalty +]



@factions
go-to: menu

= Internal factions of the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#ED2855">[+ psi_name +]</span>

The party is an amalgamation of the left-wing of the Italian political sphere, ranging from the <span style="color:#FF6961">Reformists</span> on the right, to the <span style="color:#8B0000">Communists</span> on the left, to the radicals espousing Anarchism, <span style="color:#2F2F2F">Syndicalism</span> and everything in between. However, only a select few have enough sway in the party to matter.

Overall dissent: [+ dissent_percent : dissent +]

**<span style="color:#8B0000">Communists</span>**

The <span style="color:#8B0000">Communists</span>, known also as the Comunisti, are a faction that advocate for a more far-left stance against the Kingdom, favouring extraparliamentary action and the establishment of a communist state and alignment towards the Comintern, in contrast to the other factions.

Strength: [+ communist_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ communist_dissent : dissent +]

**<span style="color:#DC143C">Maximalists</span>**

The <span style="color:#DC143C">Centre</span>, also known as the Maximalists, are the majority faction, advocating for a revolutionary approach to socialism and the establishment of a socialist state. They currently control party leadership.

Strength: [+ maximalist_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ maximalist_dissent : dissent +]

**<span style="color:#B22222">Labour</span>**

<span style="color:#B22222">Labour</span>, more primarily the General Confederation of Labour, are a minority faction in the party, generally advocating for further workers' control and the strengthening of unions.

Strength: [+ labour_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ labour_dissent : dissent +]

[? if syndicalist_active : **<span style="color:#2F2F2F">Syndicalists</span>** ?]

[? if syndicalist_active : The <span style="color:#2F2F2F">Syndicalists</span> are a minority faction within the party, splintering from Labour to advocate for strikes and workers' councils. ?]

[? if syndicalist_active : Strength: [+ syndicalist_strength : strength +] ?]

[? if syndicalist_active : Dissent: [+ syndicalist_dissent : dissent +] ?]

**Reformists**

The <span style="color:#FF6961">Reformists</span>, also known as the Riformisti, are a minority faction in the party, weakened by the split to the PSRI and favouring the establishment of socialism through parliamentary means unlike the other factions. 

Strength: [+ reformist_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ reformist_dissent : dissent +]

@figures
title: Figures and Charts
go-to: menu
view-if: not violent_revolution
on-display: {!
data = []

if (Q.pcdi_formed && Q.pcdi_seating_disp) {
    data.push({
        "id": "pcdi",
        "legend": "PCD'I",
        "name": "PCd'I",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.pcdi_seating),
    });
}

data.push({
    "id": "psi",
    "legend": "PSI",
    "name": "PSI",
    "seats": Math.round(Q.psi_seating),
});

if (Q.psu_formed && Q.psu_seating_disp) {
    data.push({
        "id": "psu",
        "legend": "PSU",
        "name": "PSU",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.psu_seating),
    });
}

if (Q.psri_collapse != 1) {
    data.push({
            "id": "psri",
            "legend": "PSRI",
            "name": "PSRI",
            "seats": Math.round(Q.psri_seating),
    });
}

if (Q.pll_formed && Q.pll_seating_disp) {
    data.push({
        "id": "pll",
        "legend": "PLL",
        "name": "PLL",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.pll_seating),
    });
}

if (Q.pri_prominent && Q.pri_seating_disp) {
    data.push({
        "id": "pri",
        "legend": "PRI",
        "name": "PRI",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.pri_seating),
    });
}

if (Q.ds_seating_disp) {
    data.push({
        "id": "ds",
        "legend": "DS",
        "name": Q.ds_name,
        "seats": Math.round(Q.ds_seating),
    });
}

data.push({
        "id": "ppi",
        "legend": "PPI",
        "name": "PPI",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.ppi_seating),
});

data.push({
    "id": "ldr",
    "legend": "LDR",
    "name": Q.ldr_name,
    "seats": Math.round(Q.ldr_seating),
});

if (Q.bn_formed === 1 && Q.bn_seating_disp) {
    data.push({
        "id": "bn",
        "legend": "BN",
        "name": "BN",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.bn_seating), 
    })
}

if (Q.ul_in_bn != 1 && Q.ul_seating_disp) {
    data.push({
        "id": "ul",
        "legend": "UL",
        "name": Q.ul_name,
        "seats": Math.round(Q.ul_seating),
    });
}

if (Q.pcs_formed) {
    data.push({
        "id": "pcs",
        "legend": "PCS",
        "name": "PCS",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.pcs_seating),
    });
}

if (Q.pnf_in_bn != 1 && Q.pnf_seating_disp) {
    data.push({
        "id": "pnf",
        "legend": "PNF",
        "name": Q.pnf_name,
        "seats": Math.round(Q.pnf_seating),
    });
}

data.push({
        "id": "other",
        "legend": "Other",
        "name": "Other",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.other_seating),
});

    if (d3 && window) {
        // get screen width
        var width = 500;
        var height = 500;
        var screenWidth = document.getElementById('content').offsetWidth;
        if (screenWidth < width - 50) {
            width = screenWidth - 50;
            height = width;
            document.getElementById("chamber").style.height = screenWidth/2 + "px";
        }
        var parliament = d3.parliament();
        parliament.width(width).height(height).innerRadiusCoef(0.4);
        parliament.enter.fromCenter(true).smallToBig(true);
        parliament.exit.toCenter(false).bigToSmall(true);
        d3.select("#chamber").datum(data).call(parliament);

        var lines = d3.linegraph(false, false,
                Q.parties,
                {'psri': '#FFC0CB', 'psi': '#ED2855', 'ldr': '#FFD700', 'ds': '#1E99C5', 'ul': '#0047AB', 'ppi': '#87CEFA', 'pnf': '#000000', 'other': '#a0a0a0', 'pcdi': '#C72F35', 'psu': '#E35A5A', 'pri': '#3CB371', 'bn': '#002d6d'},
                {'psri': 'PSRI', 'psi': 'PSI', 'ldr': Q.ldr_name, 'ds': 'DS', 'ul': Q.ul_name, 'ppi': 'PPI', 'pnf': Q.pnf_name, 'other': 'Others', 'pcdi': 'PCdI', 'psu': 'PSU', 'pri': 'PRI', 'bn': 'BN'});
        lines.width(width).height(400);
        //var svg = lines(Q.election_records);
        if (Q.election_records.length > 0) {
            d3.select("#election_history").datum(Q.election_records).call(lines);
        }
        //document.getElementById('election_history').innerHTML = svg.outerHTML;

        // party support records should not have so many ticks
        if (!Q.historical_mode || Q.game_over) {
            var lines_2 = d3.linegraph(true, true,
                Q.parties,
                {'psri': '#FFC0CB', 'psi': '#ED2855', 'ldr': '#FFD700', 'ds': '#1E99C5', 'ul': '#0047AB', 'ppi': '#87CEFA', 'pnf': '#000000', 'other': '#a0a0a0', 'pcdi': '#C72F35', 'psu': '#E35A5A', 'pri': '#3CB371', 'bn': '#002d6d'},
                {'psri': 'PSRI', 'psi': 'PSI', 'ldr': Q.ldr_name, 'ds': 'DS', 'ul': Q.ul_name, 'ppi': 'PPI', 'pnf': Q.pnf_name, 'other': 'Others', 'pcdi': 'PCdI', 'psu': 'PSU', 'pri': 'PRI', 'bn': 'BN'});
            lines_2.width(width).height(400);
            d3.select("#party_support_history").datum(Q.party_support_records).call(lines_2);
        }

        // economic stats
        var maxInflation = d3.max(Q.economic_records, d => d.inflation);
        var maxUnemployment = d3.max(Q.economic_records, d => d.unemployment);
        var minEconomicGrowth = d3.min(Q.economic_records, d => d.economicgrowth);
        var upperBound = Math.max(maxUnemployment, maxInflation) + 5;
        var lines_3 = d3.linegraph(true, true, ['inflation', 'unemployment', 'economicgrowth'],
                {'inflation': '#0000FF', 'unemployment': '#1E99C5', 'economicgrowth': '#FFD700'},
                {'inflation': 'Inflation', 'unemployment': 'Unemployment', 'economicgrowth': 'Economic Growth'},
                upperBound,
                minEconomicGrowth - 5, 21);
        lines_3.width(width).height(300);
        d3.select("#economic_history").datum(Q.economic_records).call(lines_3);
    }
!}

= Chamber of Deputies composition

{!<svg id="chamber" style="width: 500px; height: 250px;"> </svg>!}

{!<table>!}
{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#ED2855; outline: 2px; outline-style: solid;'> </div></td><td>!} **[+ psi_name +]:** {!</td><td>!} **[+ psi_seating_disp +]%** {!</td></tr>!}

[? if pcdi_formed : {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#C72F35'> </div></td> <td>!} PCd'I: {!</td><td>!} [+ pcdi_seating_disp +]% {!</td></tr>!} ?]

[? if psu_formed : {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#E35A5A'> </div></td> <td>!} PSU: {!</td><td>!} [+ psu_seating_disp +]% {!</td></tr>!} ?]

[? if not psri_collapse : {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#FFC0CB'> </div></td><td>!} PSRI: {!</td><td>!} [+ psri_seating_disp +]% {!</td></tr>!} ?]

[? if pll_formed : {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#FFD1D9'> </div></td><td>!} PLL: {!</td><td>!} [+ pll_seating_disp +]% {!</td></tr>!} ?]

[? if pri_prominent : {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#3CB371'> </div></td> <td>!} PRI: {!</td><td>!} [+ pri_seating_disp +]% {!</td></tr>!} ?]

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#1E99C5'> </div></td><td>!} [+ ds_name +]: {!</td><td>!} [+ ds_seating_disp +]% {!</td></tr>!}

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#87CEFA'> </div></td><td>!} PPI: {!</td><td>!} [+ ppi_seating_disp +]% {!</td></tr>!}

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#DCCA4A'> </div></td><td>!} [+ ldr_name +]: {!</td><td>!} [+ ldr_seating_disp +]% {!</td></tr>!}

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#00008B'> </div></td><td>!} [+ ul_name +]: {!</td><td>!} [+ ul_seating_disp +]% {!</td></tr>!}

[? if pcs_formed : {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#656573'> </div></td><td>!} PCS: {!</td><td>!} [+ pcs_seating_disp +]% {!</td></tr>!} ?]

[? if pnf_banned != 1 : {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#000000'> </div></td><td>!} [+ pnf_name +]: {!</td><td>!} [+ pnf_seating_disp +]% {!</td></tr>!} ?]

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#a0a0a0'> </div></td><td>!} Other parties: {!</td><td>!} [+ other_seating_disp +] % {!</td></tr>!}
{!</table>!}

